      "message": "just a note, when using std140 layout (which is what we use for uniform storage in vulkan and dawn), an array of float like this will actually have its elements padded out to 4 elements each. xBounds and yBounds would both then take up 96 bytes instead of 24.\n\nWe could pack the xBounds and yBounds into 3 float4s to avoid that, but it does make indexing more annoying in the VS.",
